| 9   | Oranges               | 87             | 78            |
| 10  | Watermelons           | 265            | 22            |

Total inventory capacity: $C = 1035$

---

### Mathematical Model

**Decision variables:**
$$
x_i \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0} \quad \text{for } i = 1, \ldots, 10
$$

**Objective:**
$$
\max \left(49x_1 + 30x_2 + 30x_3 + 18x_4 + 54x_5 + 27x_6 + 91x_7 + 88x_8 + 78x_9 + 22x_{10}\right)
$$

**Subject to:**
$$
282x_1 + 83x_2 + 251x_3 + 257x_4 + 88x_5 + 52x_6 + 198x_7 + 203x_8 + 87x_9 + 265x_{10} \leq 1035
$$

$$
x_i \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0} \quad \forall i = 1, \ldots, 10
$$

Where:
- $x_i$ = number of units of product $i$ to order daily
- $v_i$ = value per unit of product $i$ (see table)
- $w_i$ = weight per unit of product $i$ (see table)
- $C = 1035$ is the total inventory capacity (weight limit)[0m

